**Q1.6.2.** Using the cumulative odds associated to the system of equations in **Q1.3.3.**, provide the interpretation for `age` **by each cumulative odd**.

<!--
# BEGIN QUESTION
name: Q1-6-2-reasoning
manual: true
-->

**ANSWER:**

<!-- # BEGIN SOLUTION -->

> *Let us start with the first cumulative odd:*
\begin{align*}
\frac{P(Y_i = \texttt{Too Much} \mid X_{i, \texttt{age}},X_{i, \texttt{Norway}},X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}},X_{i, \texttt{USA}})}{P(Y_i \leq \texttt{About Right} \mid X_{i, \texttt{age}},X_{i, \texttt{Norway}},X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}},X_{i, \texttt{USA}})} &= \exp\big(-\beta_0^{(\texttt{About Right})}\big) \exp\big(\beta_1 X_{i, \texttt{Age}}\big) \\
& \qquad \exp\big(\beta_2 X_{i, \texttt{Norway}}\big) \exp\big(\beta_3 X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}}\big) \exp\big(\beta_4 X_{i, \texttt{USA}}\big).
\end{align*}
> *The interpretation of $\hat{\beta}_1$ (recall we use the estimate in our interpretations) is the following: for each 1 year increase in `age`, while holding `country` constant, the odds of believing that the government is doing `Too Much` for people in poverty versus `About Right` (or any lesser degree) increase by $(1.01 - 1) \times 100\% = 1\%$.*

> *Now, for the second cumulative odd:*
\begin{align*}
\frac{P(Y_i \geq \texttt{About Right} \mid X_{i, \texttt{age}},X_{i, \texttt{Norway}},X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}},X_{i, \texttt{USA}})}{P(Y_i = \texttt{Too Little} \mid X_{i, \texttt{age}},X_{i, \texttt{Norway}},X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}},X_{i, \texttt{USA}})} &= \exp\big(-\beta_0^{(\texttt{Too Little})}\big) \exp\big(\beta_1 X_{i, \texttt{Age}}\big) \\
& \qquad \exp\big(\beta_2 X_{i, \texttt{Norway}}\big) \exp\big(\beta_3 X_{i, \texttt{Sweden}}\big) \exp\big(\beta_4 X_{i, \texttt{USA}}\big).
\end{align*}
> *The interpretation of $\hat{\beta}_1$ is the following: for each 1 year increase in `age`, while holding `country` constant, the odds of believing that the government is doing `About Right` (or any higher degree) for people in poverty versus `Too Little` increase by $(1.01 - 1) \times 100\% = 1\%$.*

